  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The internal energy of a gas is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>.</p><p>A diatomic gas has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;translational and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;rotational degrees of freedom. A monoatomic gas has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;translational degrees of freedom.</p><p>Hence, the internal energy of the mixture&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>T</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
